            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for a peg (on a wall), then the Urdu for a socket (for a plug)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ردی",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ردی — raddī — \"waste paper; scrap\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ہم پرانے اخبار ردی میں بیچتے ہیں۔ ham purāne akhbār raddī meṅ bechte haiṅ. We sell our old newspapers as waste paper."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ردی (raddī) is usually traced to Persian raddī, \"rejected, worthless\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
